      "content": "Do not rub your eye, as this will worsen the chemical burn and embed the cleaner deeper into the tissue. Rise surfaces is a chemical irritant that can cause permanent damage, so you must immediately flush it out by holding the eyelids open under a gentle stream of clean, lukewarm water for at least 15 to 20 minutes, making sure the water reaches deep inside the lash line. Please seek immediate emergency medical attention or go to an urgent care clinic, as drain cleaner splashes often require neutralization and professional irrigation that home remedies cannot provide. Herbal eye drops are likely ineffective against such a strong chemical and could further alter the pH balance of your eye.",
